                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "43bba32b-523b-3310-bf72-51f02517edc6",
                        "entry_id": "925f0ac4-916a-3dba-8a75-2c673266451f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To cut off or slice; to sever."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a7aaa4b-8e01-49b3-8ec1-cfc10ccc7cf5",
                                "sense_id": "43bba32b-523b-3310-bf72-51f02517edc6",
                                "text": "That I as well may furnish good mens needs / With bleſſings, as detrench th'abuſed ſtore / Of thankles caytiffes; crowne true vertues deeds / With honour, and on vice my vengeance poure."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4590275f-e3e8-4dcd-aa4b-31ce02403fa0",
                                "sense_id": "43bba32b-523b-3310-bf72-51f02517edc6",
                                "text": "But these proceeding against him did not give plenary satisfaction to all, most cryed aloud for a Reformation in the Hierarchy it self, many would detrench from them their secular power, and votes in Parliament, name some were male-content unlesse the hole order were eradicated; and this was now vehemently pressed by the City Petition, now under consideration of the Committee: a mighty debate there was about this time in the House of Commons upon this Subject, and no arguments omitted which might officiate to either end; among the rest Espiscopacy had not a faster friend, nor the City Petition a stouter Antagonist, then the Lird Digby, who spake for the one and against the other no man to better purpose, and summarily thus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "963b0711-9561-46fe-8d90-0199f16a30a3",
                                "sense_id": "43bba32b-523b-3310-bf72-51f02517edc6",
                                "text": "In which instant he beheld sidelong how the cruel murtherer smote with his spear that delicate lady, and detrenched and cut the two master-veins of her neck, so as she fell dying in her blood."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ed4c756-9c37-33d8-b050-4c5c81b79b64",
                        "entry_id": "925f0ac4-916a-3dba-8a75-2c673266451f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To render something that was entrenched less thoroughly established."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "879dd258-c273-4ce1-b670-e68933c57c81",
                                "sense_id": "3ed4c756-9c37-33d8-b050-4c5c81b79b64",
                                "text": "They found themselves caught up in a mesh of arguments about entrenching, re-entrenching and detrenching, with all the relevant permutations and combinations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25815b8b-354e-4874-928d-4363178761cc",
                                "sense_id": "3ed4c756-9c37-33d8-b050-4c5c81b79b64",
                                "text": "Worthwhile amendments to some detrenched clauses affecting the Judiciary in the Republican Constitution are being studied carefully, and Bills will be laid before Parliament during the current session."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0fef641-c677-4077-8a15-559020148c8c",
                                "sense_id": "3ed4c756-9c37-33d8-b050-4c5c81b79b64",
                                "text": "How do interests coalesce, how do they achieve or fail to achieve entrenchment, how are they detrenched when their day is done?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
